---
const title = "Active Directory IAM Lab";
const description =
  "A hands-on enterprise-style identity lab built with Windows Server and Active Directory.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <title>{title} | earthlingmaeve</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <nav>
        <a href="/" class="logo">earthlingmaeve</a>

        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="/#projects">Projects</a>
          <a href="/#blog">Blog</a>
          <a href="/now">Now</a>
          <a href="/#about">About</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/earthlingmaeve">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <a href="/#projects" class="back">← Back to projects</a>

      <header class="project-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">PROJECT · IN PROGRESS</p>
        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <p class="intro">{description}</p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>What I'm building</h2>

        <p>
          I'm building a fictional enterprise environment to practice the
          identity and access management concepts that sit behind real
          Windows environments.
        </p>

        <p>
          The lab starts with Windows Server and Active Directory Domain
          Services, then expands into users, groups, organizational units,
          Group Policy, permissions, identity lifecycle management, and
          automation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Planned architecture</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Windows Server 2025 domain controller</li>
          <li>Active Directory Domain Services</li>
          <li>Integrated DNS</li>
          <li>Organizational Units based on business roles</li>
          <li>Role-based security groups</li>
          <li>Group Policy</li>
          <li>File and share permissions</li>
          <li>PowerShell identity automation</li>
          <li>Joiner / mover / leaver workflows</li>
          <li>Future Microsoft Entra ID integration</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Identity model</h2>

        <p>
          The goal is to avoid treating Active Directory as simply a
          collection of user accounts. I'll use role-based groups and an
          access model based on job responsibilities.
        </p>

        <p>
          One of the principles I'll practice throughout the lab is
          <strong>least privilege</strong>: users should receive the access
          required for their role rather than permissions being assigned
          directly to individual accounts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What I'll document</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Architecture decisions</li>
          <li>OU and group design</li>
          <li>Access-control decisions</li>
          <li>Group Policy configuration</li>
          <li>Troubleshooting and mistakes</li>
          <li>PowerShell automation</li>
          <li>Security considerations</li>
          <li>What I'd do differently in production</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Status</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Current stage:</strong> Lab environment created. AD DS is
          installed and the environment is ready for the identity design
          phase.
        </p>

        <p>
          The next milestone is creating the fictional organization,
          organizational units, users, and role-based groups.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>Built with Astro · Documented on GitHub</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family:
      Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont,
      "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #172033;
    background: #f7f8fa;
  }

  :global(a) {
    color: inherit;
  }

  header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e5ea;
  }

  nav {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .logo {
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .nav-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .nav-links a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem;
  }

  .back {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #596579;
  }

  .project-header {
    padding: 4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e5ea;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: #596579;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 2rem;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #596579;
  }

  section {
    padding: 3.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e5ea;
  }

  li {
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  footer {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
    color: #596579;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    nav {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
